      },
      "text": "São Luís to Barreirinhas"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "191384268e19613a457a817dba83c1becabf7e95afe793f0338ffb5d57b1c20b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261109-mw9omcmv",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "We leave for Barreirinhas at 7:00 a.m. The drive takes about four hours and passes local plantations.\n\nBarreirinhas is a quiet town on the banks of the Preguiças River. Just beyond town lies Lençóis Maranhenses National Park, with its white sand dunes. From March to September, blue lakes and lagoons form between the dunes.\n\nAt 2:00 p.m. we head into Lençóis Maranhenses by jeep. We’ll walk around the Blue Lagoon and swim in the lagoons. We’ll stay in the dunes until late in the evening to watch the sunset.\n\nBack in Barreirinhas, you can swim in the hotel pool, stroll along the quiet streets or spend the evening at a riverside restaurant."
    },
